From a50e4d5722133cda688f713987a547cceeeeae35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <stephen.bates@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 19:39:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ionic: allocate an address handle for UC queue pairs

ionic_create_qp() sets has_ah only for IB_QPT_RC, so a UC QP never gets
its struct ib_ud_header allocated.  ionic_modify_qp() then unconditionally
requires that header whenever IB_QP_AV is set, which it always is for a
RoCE transition to RTR:

	if (mask & IB_QP_AV) {
		if (!qp->hdr)
			return -ENOMEM;

The result is that every UC QP fails to reach RTR.  ibv_uc_pingpong
reports "Failed to modify QP to RTR" and no command is ever posted to
the device.

UC needs the same L2/L3 header as RC -- the transport differs only in
acknowledgement, not in addressing -- so extend has_ah to cover it.  All
three other users of has_ah are the matching ahid/hdr alloc and free
paths, which become symmetric for UC as a result.

Signed-off-by: Stephen Bates <stephen.bates@amd.com>
---
 drivers/infiniband/hw/ionic/ionic_controlpath.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/infiniband/hw/ionic/ionic_controlpath.c b/drivers/infiniband/hw/ionic/ionic_controlpath.c
index 9d91f7667..efe3186a1 100644
--- a/drivers/infiniband/hw/ionic/ionic_controlpath.c
+++ b/drivers/infiniband/hw/ionic/ionic_controlpath.c
@@ -2200,7 +2200,8 @@ int ionic_create_qp(struct ib_qp *ibqp, struct ib_qp_init_attr *attr,
 		return rc;
 
 	qp->sig_all = attr->sq_sig_type == IB_SIGNAL_ALL_WR;
-	qp->has_ah = attr->qp_type == IB_QPT_RC;
+	qp->has_ah = attr->qp_type == IB_QPT_RC ||
+		     attr->qp_type == IB_QPT_UC;
 
 	if (qp->has_ah) {
 		qp->hdr = kzalloc_obj(*qp->hdr);
-- 
